---
alwaysApply: true
---
When using `/fix-ticket` or SmartDeveloper subagents (`@triage`, `@context`, `@plan`,
`@dev`, `@test`, `@review`, `@docs-pr`, `@pr-fix`), ticket state lives in
`.dev-agent/{ticket-id}/` (`pipeline.json` plus numbered artifacts) in the **current
project workspace**.

Agents always read prior-stage files before starting their stage, and never skip
ahead to a later stage's file. Never proceed past a human gate without explicit
go-ahead in the conversation. The plan gate (stage 3) and the PR gate (stage 7) are
required, not optional, regardless of ticket size.

After each subagent finishes, stop and wait for engineer go-ahead before invoking the
next stage.

## Failure handling

If a subagent fails or times out, the orchestrator presents a brief error card and
**stops**. Confirm a recovery option (`retry {stage}`, `abort`, etc.) before
continuing. See `agents/shared/error-handling.md`.

Warn at **5 minutes** if a stage is still running. At **15 minutes**, treat as
timeout and wait for your confirmation.

## Platform and scope

Agents work in the **current project workspace** only. Multi-platform tickets
(Android/iOS, etc.) are scoped to the repo you have open — the agent will ask if
you want other platforms fixed and will need repo/path info. If the issue is not
in client code (backend, test env, QA repro, proxy logs), agents should tell you
what to check next rather than forcing a code change.
